 "notes": "Paper presents projected 3-year sensitivity limits (\u03ba=2, ~95% C.L.) for ALP-photon coupling g_agamma at reactor neutrino experiments (MINER, CONUS, CONNIE, \u03bd-cleus). Data points extracted from Fig. 3 (top panel) showing MINER Ge (4 kg) sensitivity curve. The limit is mass-independent (flat) for m_a \u2264 10^4 eV due to ALP scattering in detector material, peaks near m_a \u2243 4 MeV from a\u2192\u03b3\u03b3 decay, and drops sharply above m_a \u2243 10 MeV due to reactor photon flux cutoff. Paper also constrains ALP-electron coupling g_ae (Fig. 3 bottom), but primary focus and strongest new constraints are on g_agamma. Confidence is moderate (0.75) because: (1) these are projections, not measured limits; (2) data extracted from figure rather than explicit table; (3) paper discusses multiple experiments and couplings, though AxionPhoton is clearly primary. No local DM density assumption applies\u2014this is a reactor-based laboratory search, not a haloscope. | vector-trace candidate: electron_limits_with_astro.pdf colour (0.85, 0.65, 0.13), 118 pts (selected among 7) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 118))",
